The table's "extrapolated degree" column carries the anchors' value 4
because the fit has no point above them; read against the measured lower
bound (≥ 5 at m·ℓ = 21, far below the priced m·ℓ ≈ n), every n = 131 row
with admissible degree ≤ 4 is short by at least one degree at w = 1 and by
three at w = 2.2. The next cell is the same one: m·ℓ = 21 at degree 5,
which needs a host with 64 GB or more (dense closure about 72 GB at
N = 40; F4's degree-5 step above 12.6 GB) or an out-of-core closure. The
cells, draws and scorer are in place for it.
